    "description": "# Future Directions: Formal Limits of Molecular Computing\n\nThis project formalizes, in Lean 4 / Mathlib, three pillars of the \"nanotechnology\ncomputation\" moonshot, each stated as fully proved theorems (no `sorry`, only the\nstandard axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).\n\n## What was proved\n\n### `ChemicalReactionNetworks.lean` \u2014 discrete mass-action CRNs\n- **Strong monotonicity** (`Reaction.fire_add`, `Reaction.fire_mono`): surplus\n  molecules ride along untouched through any reaction.\n- **Translation invariance of reachability** (`step_shift`, `reach_shift`) and\n  **upward-monotone coverability** (`coverable_mono`) \u2014 the structural signature of\n  Petri-net / vector-addition dynamics.\n- **Conservation laws** (`mass_fire`, `mass_reach`): any balanced linear functional\n  (mass, charge, atom count) is invariant along every reachable trajectory.\n- **The fundamental limit** (`no_zero_test`): monotonicity makes it *impossible*\n  for a reaction to detect the *absence* of a species. This is the exact obstruction\n  to Turing-completeness of the exact discrete model \u2014 a register machine's zero-test\n  cannot be implemented.\n\n### `MolecularParallelism.lean` \u2014 no exponential speedup\n- **Work\u2013time bound** (`work_time_bound`): `W \u2264 T \u00b7 p`.\n- **Speedup \u2264 p** (`speedup_at_most_p`) and **volume-capped speedup**\n  (`volume_bounded_speedup`).\n- **No exponential speedup** (`no_exponential_speedup`,\n  `parallel_time_exponential`): with fixed volume and exponential work, parallel\n  time is unbounded \u2014 molecular parallelism is a constant-factor win, not an\n  exponential one.\n\n### `StorageCapacity.lean` \u2014 information-theoretic limits\n- **Storage capacity** (`storage_capacity`): `k` two-state molecules \u21d2 \u2264 `2^k`\n  configurations; **bit lower bound** (`bits_lower_bound`): distinguishing `N`\n  inputs needs \u2265 `log\u2082 N` bits.\n- **Kolmogorov-style volume bound** (`kolmogorov_volume_lower_bound`): description\n  length (\u2248 volume) \u2265 `log\u2082(#behaviors)`.\n- **Density sanity check** (`dna_density_bound`, `dna_density_needs_more`):\n  `2^59 < 10^18 \u2264 2^60`.\n\n## Natural next steps\n\n1. **Turing-completeness with error.** The `no_zero_test` obstruction is exactly why\n   *exact* CRNs are only as strong as Petri nets (decidable coverability). Formalize\n   the Soloveichik\u2013Cook\u2013Winfree\u2013Bruck construction: stochastic CRNs that simulate a\n   register machine with unbounded time and vanishing error probability recover full\n   Turing power. This requires a probabilistic/continuous-time layer on top of the\n   present discrete semantics.\n\n2. **Decidability of coverability.** Prove Karp\u2013Miller / the well-quasi-order\n   (Dickson's lemma, already in Mathlib) implies coverability of the CRN model is\n   decidable \u2014 a positive counterpart to `no_zero_test`.\n\n3. **Reachability invariants via conservation.** Use `mass_reach` to derive\n   non-reachability certificates (Farkas-style): if no nonnegative combination of\n   conserved functionals separates source from target, additional siphon/trap\n   invariants are needed.\n\n4. **Tight time hierarchy.** Strengthen `no_exponential_speedup` to a genuine\n   time\u2013volume tradeoff `T(n) \u00b7 V \u2265 c \u00b7 W(n)`, and connect `W(n)` to circuit or\n   Turing-machine complexity of the target function.\n\n5. **Kolmogorov complexity proper.** Replace the counting surrogate in\n   `kolmogorov_volume_lower_bound` with a formal prefix-free Kolmogorov complexity\n   (an incompressibility development), giving a literal \"minimum CRN volume \u2265 K(f)\".\n\n6. **Mass-action ODE limit.** Bridge the discrete model to deterministic\n   mass-action ODEs and formalize the classical result that the deficiency-zero\n   networks have well-behaved (complex-balanced) steady states.\n",
