    "description": "# Future Directions \u2014 Bruhat order and closure of orbit strata\n\nThis cycle established the order-theoretic backbone of the statement *\"Bruhat order\npreserves closure relations for orbit strata on a product of flag manifolds\"*: the\nEhresmann rank criterion is a genuine partial order (its rank matrix determines the\npermutation), it is inversion-invariant, it has explicit extremes, and it transports to\na product order via the two-projection map `w \u21a6 (w, w\u207b\u00b9)`. Building on the surviving\nresults and the failure analysis, we propose the following conjectures.\n\n## 1. The closure order is exactly the componentwise Bruhat order \u2014 with matched gradings\n\n**Conjecture.** For the two-projection parametrisation of orbit strata, `O\u2081 \u2286 closure O\u2082`\nholds if and only if the parametrising pairs satisfy the componentwise Bruhat order, *and*\nthe codimension of a stratum equals the sum of the two Coxeter lengths of its parameters.\n\n*The key insight is* that the inversion length is a rank function for the Bruhat order, so\nthe componentwise order on pairs is graded by the *sum* of the two lengths; a closure\nrelation can only add codimension, which forces the order to be the componentwise one with\nadditive grading. *Why now?* The transpose identity `rk w\u207b\u00b9 i j = rk w j i` proved this\ncycle makes the two projections carry perfectly compatible, additively-graded orders, so\nthe additive-codimension refinement is now within reach rather than conjectural folklore.\n\n## 2. Length monotonicity strengthens to strict length monotonicity on covers\n\n**Conjecture.** If `u < v` in the Bruhat order then `len u < len v`, and every covering\nrelation `u \u22d6 v` increases the length by exactly one.\n\n*The key insight is* that the rank matrix changes by a controlled amount across a single\ntransposition, so the length gap along a saturated chain telescopes to the number of steps.\n*Why now?* We have both the rank criterion and an independent inversion-length statistic\nformalised on the same objects (`rk` and `len`), so the two can finally be compared step by\nstep rather than only at the extreme points (identity and reversal).\n\n## 3. Self-duality of the orbit poset under `w \u21a6 w\u2080 w`\n\n**Conjecture.** Multiplication by the reversal permutation `w\u2080` is an order-reversing\ninvolution of the Bruhat order, and hence the product orbit poset is self-dual: the closure\nposet is anti-isomorphic to itself.\n\n*The key insight is* that `w\u2080` swaps the roles of \"smallest positions/values\" and \"largest\npositions/values\", turning the maximal rank matrix into the minimal one. *Why now?* With the\nidentity and reversal already pinned down as the two extremes of the order, the involution\nsending one extreme to the other is the natural next structural symmetry to certify.\n\n## 4. Rank-matrix rigidity governs the whole closure lattice\n\n**Conjecture.** Two orbit strata coincide if and only if their rank matrices agree\nentrywise, and the closure lattice of strata embeds order-preservingly into the lattice of\nentrywise-dominated integer matrices.\n\n*The key insight is* that antisymmetry \u2014 \"the rank matrix determines the permutation\" \u2014 is\nnot just a technical nicety but the reason the closure relation is a *lattice* order rather\nthan a mere preorder. *Why now?* The determinacy result is now a theorem, so the passage\nfrom \"orbits\" to \"matrices\" is a faithful encoding, and the lattice structure can be studied\npurely combinatorially.\n\n## 5. Inversion-freeness detects the dense open stratum\n\n**Conjecture.** A stratum is the unique dense (open) orbit of its factor exactly when the\ncorresponding parameter is inversion-free, and dually the unique closed orbit corresponds to\nthe reversal parameter.\n\n*The key insight is* that the Bruhat-minimal element is precisely the unique inversion-free\npermutation, so \"minimal in closure order\" and \"no inversions\" are the same condition. *Why\nnow?* This cycle proved `bruhat_bot_iff_len_zero`, tying the order-theoretic minimum to the\nvanishing of the inversion statistic; extending it from the extreme stratum to a full\nopen/closed dichotomy is the immediate structural sequel.\n",
