    "description": "# Future Directions \u2014 The Topology of Argumentation (VI): the existence gap for stable extensions\n\nThis cycle (contrarian mode) attacks the **existence gap** left open by the\nprevious cycle's `Catalog/Novelty/ArgumentationStable.lean`:\n\n> Unlike preferred extensions, **stable extensions need not exist.**\n\nNew self-contained file: `Catalog/Novelty/ArgumentationStableGap.lean`\n(Lean 4 / Mathlib `v4.28.0`, no `sorry`, axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice`,\n`Quot.sound`).\n\n## Bold conjectures, settled\n\nWe formulated four bold conjectures on the existence of stable extensions and\nsettled each \u2014 proving two and disproving two.\n\n| # | Conjecture | Verdict | Theorem |\n|---|------------|---------|---------|\n| C1 | Every finite framework has a stable extension | **DISPROVED** | `no_stable_cycle3` |\n| C2 | Every preferred extension is stable | **DISPROVED** | `cycle3_preferred_not_stable` |\n| C3 | Every finite symmetric irreflexive framework has a stable extension | **PROVED** | `stable_exists_of_finite_symmetric_irrefl` |\n| C4 | Symmetry alone suffices for existence (C3 without irreflexivity) | **DISPROVED** | `no_stable_reflAF` |\n\n### C1 / C2 \u2014 the odd cycle refutations\n\nThe directed 3-cycle `cycle3 : 0 \u2192 1 \u2192 2 \u2192 0` (`R a b \u2194 b = a + 1` on `Fin 3`) is\nirreflexive (`cycle3_irreflexive`) and *not* symmetric (`cycle3_not_symmetric`).\n\n* `no_stable_cycle3` \u2014 the 3-cycle has **no** stable extension, refuting C1.\n* `stable_cycle3_ncard` \u2014 quantitatively, `#{stable extensions} = 0` (contrast\n  the count `n` for the complete conflict graph in `ArgumentationStable.lean`).\n* `cycle3_admissible_empty`, `cycle3_preferred_empty` \u2014 the empty set is the\n  unique admissible set, hence a preferred extension of the 3-cycle.\n* `cycle3_empty_not_stable`, `cycle3_preferred_not_stable` \u2014 but `\u2205` is not\n  stable, so `stable \u228a preferred` is a **strict** inclusion (refuting C2 and\n  sharpening `ArgumentationStable.stable_preferred`).\n\n### C3 \u2014 existence on the symmetric side\n\n* `exists_maximalConflictFree` \u2014 on a finite type a maximal conflict-free set\n  (a facet of `K(AF)`) always exists.\n* `maximalConflictFree_stable_of_symmetric` \u2014 in a symmetric irreflexive\n  framework every facet is stable (re-proved self-contained).\n* `stable_exists_of_finite_symmetric_irrefl` \u2014 hence **every finite symmetric\n  irreflexive framework admits a stable extension**, closing the existence gap\n  on the symmetric side.\n\n### C4 \u2014 irreflexivity is necessary\n\n* `no_stable_of_reflexive` \u2014 any nonempty framework in which every argument\n  attacks itself has no stable extension (only `\u2205` is conflict-free, and `\u2205`\n  cannot dominate a nonempty universe).\n* `no_stable_reflAF` \u2014 the concrete symmetric one-argument self-attack framework\n  `reflAF` therefore has no stable extension: symmetry alone does not save C3;\n  irreflexivity is genuinely needed.\n\n## Computational evidence\n\n`ComputationalEvidence.md` records the brute-force enumeration over all subsets\nof `Fin 3` that motivated these results: the 3-cycle has `1` admissible (the\nempty set), `1` preferred, and `0` stable extensions, while the complete graph\n`K_3` has `3` stable extensions.\n\n## Open directions\n\n* **Characterize existence in general.** Give a purely combinatorial criterion\n  (beyond symmetry) on `(A, R)` guaranteeing a stable extension; e.g. relate it\n  to the absence of odd directed cycles among self-defended arguments, or to the\n  independence complex of the underlying conflict graph having a full-dimensional\n  facet.\n* **Counting the gap.** For random or structured frameworks, study\n  `#{preferred} \u2212 #{stable}` as a numeric invariant of the \"abstention\" forced\n  by odd cycles.\n* **Topology of non-existence.** Interpret the vanishing of stable extensions\n  (`stable_cycle3_ncard = 0`) homologically: relate it to the reduced homology\n  of `K(AF)` for directed (non-symmetric) frameworks, extending the Euler bridge\n  of `ArgumentationSymmetric`/`ArgumentationStable` beyond the symmetric case.\n",
